    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Two students calculate $3568+2417$. Use an estimate to judge each answer.\n(a) Ana records $5985$.\n(b) Jo records $6985$.",
        "solution_text": "Round both numbers to the nearest hundred.\n$3568+2417\\approx3600+2400=6000$\n(a) $5985$ is close to $6000$, so it is reasonable.\n(b) $6985$ is about $1000$ above the estimate, so it is not reasonable. The estimate helps find the size error."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Use an estimate to judge each answer for $9346-2788$.\n(a) $6558$\n(b) $7558$",
        "solution_text": "Round both numbers to the nearest hundred.\n$9346-2788\\approx9300-2800=6500$\n(a) $6558$ is close to $6500$, so it is reasonable.\n(b) $7558$ is about $1000$ above the estimate, so it is not reasonable."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Use place value to check each recorded result.\n(a) $8042-975=767$\n(b) Four lots of $507$ are added and the total is recorded as $228$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $8042-975\\approx8000-1000=7000$\nThe answer should be in the thousands. The recorded $767$ is far too small.\n$\\begin{aligned}\\text{(b)}\\quad &\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}507+507+507+507\\\\&\\approx500+500+500+500\\\\&=2000\\end{aligned}$\nThe total should be about $2000$, so $228$ is far too small. The place-value check reveals the error."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) A student writes $16\\,438+5789=22\\,226$. The estimate is close. Check the ones digit.\n(b) Another student writes $18\\,427-6938=11\\,499$. An estimate gives about $11\\,500$, and the ones digit is correct. Do these checks prove the answer is exact? Explain, then find the exact answer.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $16\\,438+5789\\approx16\\,400+5800=22\\,200$\nBut $8+9=17$, so the sum must end in $7$, not $6$. The recorded answer is wrong.\n(b) An estimate and the final digit do not check every digit. They support the size and ones digit, but do not prove the exact answer.\n$18\\,427-6938=11\\,489$\nThe recorded $11\\,499$ is close to the estimate and ends correctly in $9$, but its tens digit is wrong."
      }
    ],
